        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3}{7}$",
          "worked": "Let $E$ be the event that the sum is even and $U$ the event that at least one die shows $1$. Within $U$, the equally likely ordered outcomes are $(1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,4),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1)$. Of these, $(1,1),(1,3),(3,1)$ have an even sum.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(E\\mid U)&=\\frac{|E\\cap U|}{|U|}\\\\P(E\\mid U)&=\\frac{3}{7}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
